.TH BC250\-PADDLES 1 "2026-10-24" "bc250-paddles 0.1.0" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
bc250\-paddles \- L4/R4 of 8BitDo Ultimate 2C pads as Steam back buttons over the 2.4 GHz receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bc250\-paddles
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bc250\-paddles
sets and removes an SDL mapping in the
.B SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG
environment variable of Steam. With it, Steam Input sees L4 and R4 of an
8BitDo Ultimate 2C Wireless on its 2.4 GHz receiver as two independent back
buttons (paddle2 and paddle1, shown as L5 and R5 in the controller test).
.PP
The receiver sends L4/R4 only in DInput mode, when it shows up as USB
.I 2dc8:301c
with an input device. Steam builds an automatic mapping without them there and
ignores, then overwrites, the
.I SDL_GamepadBind
entry in
.IR config.vdf .
A mapping from the environment variable is honoured.
.PP
One mapping covers any number of pads, because every pad + receiver set has the
same identity.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
The pad on its 2.4 GHz receiver, not on a cable and not over Bluetooth.
.IP \(bu 2
Firmware that allows DInput. Verified with pad 1.06 and receiver 1.00. With pad
1.09 and receiver 1.03 switching to DInput does not work.
.IP \(bu 2
The pad in DInput mode (Home + B; back to XInput with Home + X).
.IP \(bu 2
L4/R4 not remapped inside the pad.
.IP \(bu 2
Steam started after
.BR on .
For native Steam in Gaming Mode, log out or reboot.
.PP
In DInput mode the pad does not rumble: the kernel exposes no force feedback
for it and the firmware ignores the output report.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Shows whether the mapping is set for each detected Steam installation, whether
the running Steam has it in its environment, which mapping Steam's
.I logs/controller.txt
last reports for
.IR 2dc8/301c ,
and the 8BitDo pads with their mode and receiver serial. The default command.
.TP
.B on
Sets the mapping. Native Steam: writes
.I ~/.config/environment.d/90\-bc250\-paddles.conf
and calls
.BR "systemctl \-\-user set\-environment" .
Flatpak Steam: adds the variable to the user override of
.IR com.valvesoftware.Steam ,
and removes it from
.I unset\-environment
if an earlier override listed it there. A different value already set by
somebody else is not overwritten.
.TP
.B off
Removes only what
.B on
set. Other Flatpak overrides and foreign values stay.
.TP
.B mapping
Prints the bare SDL mapping.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " \fInative\fR|\fIflatpak\fR|\fIall\fR"
Which installation to act on. Default: the detected ones.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Prints what would be done and changes nothing.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lang " \fIpl\fR|\fIen\fR"
Message language. Without it, taken from
.BR BC250_LANG ,
then from the locale; anything unrecognised means English.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Short help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The
.B status
command returns:
.TP
.B 0
The mapping is set in every detected installation.
.TP
.B 1
The mapping is not set, or no Steam was found.
.TP
.B 2
The mapping is set in some installations only.
.PP
The other commands return 0 on success and 1 on error.
.SH PRIVILEGES
None. Every change lives in the home directory and survives image updates on
atomic distributions such as Bazzite.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BC250_LANG
Message language
.RI ( pl
or
.IR en )
when
.B \-\-lang
is not given.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " FLATPAK_USER_DIR
Honoured for the locations of
.I environment.d
and the Flatpak overrides.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/environment.d/90\-bc250\-paddles.conf
The variable for native Steam.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/flatpak/overrides/com.valvesoftware.Steam
The Flatpak user override that carries the variable.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Steam/logs/controller.txt
Steam's controller log, read by
.B status
(Flatpak:
.IR ~/.var/app/com.valvesoftware.Steam/.local/share/Steam/logs/controller.txt ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Set the mapping and check it after restarting Steam:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-paddles on
bc250\-paddles status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Only for Flatpak Steam, preview first:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-paddles on \-\-target flatpak \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Undo by hand:
.PP
.RS
.EX
rm ~/.config/environment.d/90\-bc250\-paddles.conf
systemctl \-\-user unset\-environment SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Hand edits of
.I SDL_GamepadBind
in
.I config.vdf
do not work for this device: Steam replaces them with its automatic mapping
when it exits.
.PP
In XInput mode
.RI ( 2dc8:310a )
the receiver does not send L4/R4 at all; no mapping can help there.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR environment.d (5),
.BR flatpak\-override (1),
.BR bc250\-wcm (1)
.SH BUGS
Reports:
.UR https://github.com/zvgelo/bc250-tool-kit/issues
.UE
